  "methodology": "Ranks are EduRank.org world subject ranks (lower = better) as displayed on 2026-07-13 — a citation/bibliometric aggregator, not an official or accreditation body; treat each as one indicator, not ground truth. Rows are ordered by Computer Science (CSE) world rank; sorting by another subject reorders the list materially (e.g. TUM #17, RWTH #35, KIT #44 lead on Software Engineering). English-taught master availability, non-EU tuition and the application route were separately verified against each university's admissions pages, DAAD and state ministries for 2025–26. Tuition: only Baden-Württemberg (€1,500/semester, non-EU) and Bavaria charge non-EU master fees — and Bavaria's is optional per university, so TUM charges €4,000–6,000/sem and FAU follows from 2027 while LMU and most others stay tuition-free; every other state is tuition-free apart from a ~€150–384 administrative semester fee (often including a transport ticket).",
  "caveats": [
    "EduRank is bibliometric, not a government/accreditation body — these are ordinal positions, not quality scores; a 10-rank gap is not a fixed quality gap.",
    "Charité is a medical university with no CS/AI/Data master; EduRank ranks it via medical-informatics/bioinformatics output — kept for source fidelity.",
    "English-master availability, tuition and application route were current at 2026-07; verify on the university's admissions page before applying — Bavaria's tuition rules and programme intakes are changing.",
